/** EVERY PERFORMANCE FUNCTION, BY ITS IDENTIFIER, WITH THE TEST THAT PINS IT — step 3.c.
 *
 *  GENERATED by "Calculation Module code/scripts/build-nw-function-tests.py PF". Do not hand-edit: the
 *  code is the only copy, and this file is a printout of it. Re-run that script after adding a
 *  function, and the new row appears here with the test that covers it.
 *
 *  WHY IT EXISTS. His seven steps, run on 2026-10-01, found that only 2 of the module's 34 functions
 *  was named by its identifier in any test. The functions were not untested — 91 door tests run
 *  through them and pass — but every one of those tests names the FIGURES it checks, never the
 *  functions. So the trace worked in one direction only: from a figure you could reach its proof, and
 *  from a function identifier you could reach nothing.
 *
 *  That is objective 3 of the calculation module, in his words: *an architecture that lets anyone
 *  trace a wrong number to its engine and formula in one minute.* One minute means one hop, and this
 *  table is the hop. Search any MK-NW-F- identifier and you land here, on the file that declares it
 *  and the test that exercises it.
 *
 *  The table is checked, not just printed: each row's source file must exist and must really carry
 *  that identifier, and each named test must exist. A row that goes stale fails the build.
 */
